-- Master : It stores system-level information such as login accounts and configuration settings

-- Model : This database acts as a template. Whenever a new database is created, SQL Server copies the structure from the model.

-- MSDB : It is used for SQL Server Agent jobs, scheduling, and maintenance tasks

-- TEMPDB : This a temporary database used to store temporary objects and intermediate query results. It is recreated every time SQL Server restarts.

